forge_idol/native/layers.py, denoiser.py, decoder.py and birefnet.py, and forge_idol/preprocess.py, gaussian.py and
camera.py, are adapted from the Idol SDK (https://github.com/speridlabs/idol-sdk), Copyright Speridlabs, licensed under
the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE). The denoiser notes that it adapts HuggingFace Diffusers' Wan transformer,
Copyright 2025 The Wan Team and The HuggingFace Team, also under the Apache License 2.0.

Changes from the Idol SDK: the TensorDict and plyfile dependencies are removed, every Forge Neo layer casts its weights
to the type of its input, and the attention always uses PyTorch's scaled dot product attention.

forge_idol/native/turbo.py applies the phase LoRAs of speridlabs/idol-turbo (Apache License 2.0), following its turbo.py.

forge_idol/spz.py writes the SPZ format by Niantic Labs (https://github.com/nianticlabs/spz, MIT License), following its
load-spz.cc.

forge_idol/mesh.py is adapted from ComfyUI's comfy_extras/nodes_gaussian_splat.py (https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI),
licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0, which the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 may be combined with.
Changes: the density is evened out, closed and filled into a solid before the surface is extracted, thin Gaussians get a
minimum thickness, and the GPU paths and progress reporting are gone.

The structure of the Forge Neo integration follows minimax-h3-forge-neo by the same author.
